@startuml libtetrisbrain_gameplay_sequence

!theme plain

skinparam backgroundColor #FFF9FC
skinparam defaultFontName "Avenir Next"
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 14
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #756A83
  ArrowThickness 1.6
  ParticipantBorderColor #8B7E9F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontColor #40364D
  LifeLineBorderColor #C8BFD3
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F3EDF7
  GroupBorderColor #C8BFD3
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFFDFE
  GroupHeaderFontColor #604978
  NoteBorderColor #9FC5A7
  NoteBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  NoteFontColor #3F6848
  DividerBackgroundColor #F0E7FA
  DividerBorderColor #B69ACF
  DividerFontColor #604978
}

title <size:22><b>libtetrisbrain Game Step</b></size>\n<size:14>Pure game logic called by the authoritative server</size>

participant "Player or\nRoom Ticker" as Input #DDF3F5
participant "Game Server\n(tetrisd)" as Server #F9E2DC
participant "Pure Logic\n(libtetrisbrain)" as Brain #E9E2F7
participant "Caller-owned\nBoard + Piece" as State #DFF3E4

note over Server, State
tetrisd owns the room mutex and all game state.
libtetrisbrain performs no I/O and stores no state.
end note

== 1. Apply an action ==

Input -> Server: MOVE / ROTATE / SOFT DROP / gravity tick
Server -> Server: Lock room mutex
Server -> Brain: Call movement, rotation, or drop function
Brain -> State: Read current board and piece
Brain -> Brain: Test candidate cells for collisions

note over Brain, State #FFF3CD
MOVE commits only a valid candidate.
ROTATE tries SRS wall kicks.
SOFT DROP uses gravity_tick.
HARD DROP repeats downward movement,
then tetrisd enters the lock phase directly.
end note

alt Piece can continue
  Brain -> State: Update active piece
  Brain --> Server: BRAIN_OK
  Server -> Server: Unlock room mutex
  Server --> Input: Broadcast authoritative STATE
else Move or rotation is blocked
  Brain --> Server: BRAIN_BLOCKED
  Server -> Server: Unlock room mutex
  Server --> Input: Keep previous STATE
else Gravity or soft drop reports landing
  Brain --> Server: BRAIN_LOCKED

  == 2. Lock, clear, and score ==

  Server -> Brain: piece_stamp(board, piece)
  Brain -> State: Bake four piece cells into board
  Server -> Brain: board_clear_lines(board)
  Brain -> State: Remove full rows and compact downward
  Brain --> Server: Lines cleared (0-4)
  Server -> Brain: score_on_clear(lines, level)
  Brain --> Server: NES-style points
  Server -> Brain: level_from_lines(total)\ngravity_interval_ms(level)
  Brain --> Server: New level and ticker interval

  == 3. Spawn the next piece ==

  Server -> Brain: piece_spawn(next type)
  Brain -> State: Return fixed spawn transform
  Server -> Brain: piece_is_valid(board, new piece)

  alt Spawn position is free
    Brain --> Server: true
    Server -> State: Store new active piece
    Server -> Server: Unlock room mutex
    Server --> Input: Broadcast new STATE
  else Spawn position overlaps the stack
    Brain --> Server: false
    Server -> Server: Mark game over
    Server -> Server: Unlock room mutex
    Server --> Input: Broadcast final STATE
  end
end

== Optional Battle Royale transform ==

Input -> Server: Ability or garbage event
Server -> Server: Lock room mutex
Server -> Brain: Apply pure board transform
Brain -> State: Update caller-owned board
Brain --> Server: Return
Server -> Server: Unlock room mutex
Server --> Input: Broadcast authoritative STATE

@enduml
